<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 19 September, from 1356 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1356 <span class="tih-ago">670 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Black Prince captures King John II at Poitiers</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edward the Black Prince's outnumbered army defeated the French at Poitiers and captured King John II. His huge ransom and the chaos that followed brought France to the brink of collapse.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jamestown.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1676 <span class="tih-ago">350 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nathaniel Bacon's rebels burn Jamestown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rebels led by Nathaniel Bacon burned Virginia's capital, Jamestown, in a revolt against Governor Berkeley. Their alliance of poor whites, servants and enslaved Africans alarmed the colony's elite.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamestown">Jamestown</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1796 <span class="tih-ago">230 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Washington's Farewell Address is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Washington announced he would not seek a third term in an address printed in a Philadelphia newspaper. He warned against party faction and permanent foreign alliances.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1881 <span class="tih-ago">145 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President James Garfield dies 79 days after being shot</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Garfield died of infection and complications from the wound inflicted by Charles Guiteau. His doctors' unsterile probing of the wound almost certainly contributed to his death.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1991 <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hikers find Ötzi the Iceman in the Alps</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two German hikers found a body in the ice on the Austrian-Italian border. Ötzi proved to be a man who died some 5,300 years ago, killed by an arrow, with his clothes and tools preserved.</p></div></li></ol>
